AAudio: a stream that fails to start again on resume is rebuilt

Android freezes an app that stays in the background, and the audio server then closes its AAudio streams
("AAudioClientTracker ... close frozen AAudio stream"). No error callback reaches the frozen app, so when it comes
back ResumeOneDevice's AAudioStream_requestStart fails with AAUDIO_ERROR_DISCONNECTED, only sets the error, and the
device plays silence from then on. ResumeOneDevice now flags the error as AAUDIO_errorCallback does, and
AAUDIO_PlayDevice's RecoverAAudioDevice builds a new stream.

Not in SDL 3.4.18 or SDL main as of 2026-11-02. Applies after 0001 (SDL main's 36864b6), with which a stream that
cannot be built again leaves the device's buffer sizes as they were instead of crashing.

--- a/src/audio/aaudio/SDL_aaudio.c
+++ b/src/audio/aaudio/SDL_aaudio.c
@@ -528,6 +528,11 @@
             if (res != AAUDIO_OK) {
                 LOGI("SDL Failed AAudioStream_requestStart %d", res);
                 SDL_SetError("%s : %s", SDL_FUNCTION, ctx.AAudio_convertResultToText(res));
+                // A stream that can't start again stays silent, and no error callback reports it: the audio server
+                // closes the streams of an app frozen in the background, and its requestStart then fails with
+                // AAUDIO_ERROR_DISCONNECTED. Flag it as AAUDIO_errorCallback does, so PlayDevice builds a new stream.
+                SDL_SetAtomicInt(&hidden->error_callback_triggered, (int) res);
+                SDL_SignalSemaphore(hidden->semaphore);  // in case we're blocking in WaitDevice.
             }
         }
     }
